{
  "requirement": "An execution error returns `Err` rather than a `Fingerprinted` containing a\ncompleted answer.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. When execution fails, `verify` must return `Err`. It must not return a `Fingerprinted` that holds a completed answer. The reviewed tests cover the execution-error classes the SDK can produce, and each one asserts `Err`.\n\n- **Missing agent:** `validation_tests.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` has `verify` return `Err(ValidationError::NoAgentConfigured)`. It also asserts that no record was stored and no reads happened. After an agent is attached, the same validator returns a normal answer.\n- **Failure inside the callback:** in `validation_tests.rs#fn[resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments]`, a read of a missing node inside the criterion callback makes `verify` return `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"missing\"))`. No records are stored.\n- **Criterion decode failure:** `validation_tests.rs#fn[criterion_decode_errors_are_execution_errors_and_false_is_a_completed_answer]` feeds non-JSON content to a criterion. `verify` returns `Err(ValidationError::Output)` and nothing is stored. The same test shows that a legitimate `false` answer is still returned as `Ok`. That rules out an implementation that turns every negative result into an error.\n- **Criterion errors, resolution errors and graph errors:** `contracts.rs#fn[loading_execution_resolution_and_saving_failures_do_not_publish_answers]` makes `verify` return `Err(Graph(\"execute\"))` when the criterion itself fails. It returns `Err(Graph(\"missing\"))` when a read targets a missing node and `Err(Graph(\"edges\"))` when edge lookup fails. Storage stays empty and no writes occur.\n- **Related non-publication cases:** these tests cover load and store failures, which fall under the evidence requirements rather than this one, but they also show that no answer is published on failure.\n  - `contracts.rs#fn[serialization_failure_leaves_the_existing_record_unchanged]` checks that the existing record is left unchanged.\n  - `contracts.rs#fn[typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence]` checks that decode errors are reported on load.\n  - `storage.rs#fn[malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors]` checks that malformed records are reported as errors.\n\nI found no credible way for an execution error to come back as a completed `Fingerprinted` that these assertions would accept. The `matches!` checks on `Err` variants would fail if `Ok` were returned. The no-store checks add a second guard. All the tests carry the `{test}` reference to the requirement, so there is no marking gap.",
  "references": "58065e4f3a0f3ab4ef65ddff3edd1faf5524feeb66a41e31c73dcd1b307202dc",
